// TRIPWIRE MINE bore — the charge, seated 12 px inside the wall.
//
// This def exists for one reason: DEPTH. `shatter` launches its fragments
// radially away from the effect centre, and there is no argument that aims
// them. Detonated on the wall's face, half the chunks fly into the rock and
// settle; detonated a foot inside it, "radially outward" and "out of the
// wall, along the beam, at whoever broke it" are the same direction. So the
// charge is not fired where the chisel stopped — it is emitted from there
// with `offset: 12`, which runs along the emission heading, i.e. inward.
// Spawn displacement is never terrain-checked, so it seats cleanly inside
// solid rock.
//
// It has no collide lists, so being buried is inert: it can't be blocked to
// death, and with no terrain list there is no `explode_on_ground` to kill
// it early. It sits for one tick and lets go.
//
// **`speed` is 0.2 and not 0, and it is not a travel speed.** A particle's
// facing is the atan2 of its spawn velocity, and atan2(0, 0) is zero — so a
// charge with no speed detonates believing it points due east, and every
// `emit` in the effect it invokes is aimed from that. It did not matter
// while the tear only shattered: those fragments fly radially and need no
// heading. It matters now that the tear also throws spall back down the
// beam (particles/tripmine_shrapnel.json5). 0.2 px/frame is enough for both
// velocity components to survive Fp truncation at any angle (~0.3 deg of
// resolution, against the 1.4 deg an angle unit can express even in
// principle), and it buys no motion at all: the bore is buried in rock, so
// its first look-ahead is blocked, and a blocked particle with no killing
// terrain list parks where it stands before moving. The charge still goes
// off at exactly `offset: 12`.
{
  "legacy": { "particle_class": true },
  "physics": {
    "gravity": 0,
    "damping": 1,
    "pushed_by_blasts": false,
    "ccd": false
  },
  "radius": 0,
  "collide": {
    "projectiles": false
  },
  "speed": 0.2,
  "speed_variance": 0,
  "spawn_jitter": 0,
  "fuse": { "ticks": 1, "variance": 0 },
  "on": {
    "fuse": [
      "tripmine_tear",
      { "remove": {} }
    ]
  },
  "anim": { "frames": 0 },
  "presentation": {
    "color_index": -1,
    "splinter_color_index": 0,
    "sprite_wl": { "start": -1 }
  }
}
